 "answer_text": "Found 5 pubmed records, 1 medgen record, 1 literature entity record and 5 clinical trial records for Marfan syndrome [13][14][74][75][76][77][78][79][80][81][82][83]. \n\nMarfan syndrome (MFS) is a multisystem connective tissue disease with autosomal dominant inheritance, mainly caused by FBN1 gene mutation, with widely varying clinical manifestations [1]. \n\nClinical Features\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [2], Arachnodactyly [3], Astigmatism [4], Ectopia lentis [5], Esotropia [6], Exotropia [7], Pes planus [8], Glaucoma [9], Congestive heart failure [10], Hypertropia [11] and Micrognathia [12]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [13]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [76]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [78]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [80]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [82]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [14]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Pneumothorax [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Emphysema [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Retinal detachment [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Retrognathia [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Scoliosis [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Spondylolisthesis [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Strabismus [2